      "ruleId": "ssc-e7b42571-af17-4f20-bec0-193a136b1fde",
      "title": "Insertion of Sensitive Information Into Sent Data in at.yawk.lz4:lz4-java",
      "description": "Affected versions of at.yawk.lz4:lz4-java, net.jpountz.lz4:lz4, org.lz4:lz4-java, and org.lz4:lz4-pure-java are vulnerable to Insertion of Sensitive Information Into Sent Data. In lz4-java's pure-Java decompressor implementations (safeInstance(), unsafeInstance(), fastestJavaInstance(), fastDecompressor()), insufficient clearing of the output buffer allows a crafted compressed input to copy from uninitialized regions of a reused buffer\u2014potentially leaking residual or sensitive data. The JNI-based safeDecompressor is not affected. Users who reuse buffers without zeroing them before decompression are at risk.",
